 "questions": [
  {
   "id": "Q-01",
   "status": "ANSWERED — DR-001",
   "fault": [
    "F-07",
    "F-20"
   ],
   "trigger": "step-4 matrix walk",
   "text": "CRITICAL: Release() at channel.go:215 sets conns=nil, closes idle conns channel, iterates idle conns \u2014 but NEVER closes connReqs waiter channels. Goroutines blocked in Get() on <-req at channel.go:139 hang forever after pool termination. Pool terminal does not synchronize with Waiter lifecycle (PA-21). Fix: close each connReqs channel so waiters receive zero value and return ErrMaxActiveConnReached. Includes UV-Release-duplication, UV-Release-out-of-order, UV-Release-contradiction, UV-Release-commission."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-02",
   "status": "ANSWERED — DR-002",
   "fault": [
    "F-12",
    "F-14",
    "F-17"
   ],
   "trigger": "step-3 checklist",
   "text": "Put integrity: no ownership tracking or duplicate detection. UV-Put-loss: caller crashes without returning connection \u2014 openingConns stays elevated, pool capacity permanently reduced. UV-Put-duplication: caller returns same connection twice \u2014 first Put succeeds, second may corrupt waiter delivery. UV-Put-commission: pool accepts any connection regardless of origin. From run2 Q-02/Q-03/Q-06."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-03",
   "status": "ANSWERED — DR-003",
   "fault": [
    "F-04",
    "F-15"
   ],
   "trigger": "step-4 matrix walk",
   "text": "Put after Release: conns is nil so Put calls c.Close(conn) at channel.go:190. Close() then checks c.close==nil and is a silent no-op \u2014 the connection is leaked, openingConns is not decremented (already stale). No guard prevents Put on a closed pool from leaking connections. UV-Put-out-of-order covers the out-of-order arrival of Put after Release."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-04",
   "status": "ANSWERED — DR-004",
   "fault": [
    "F-03"
   ],
   "trigger": "step-4 matrix walk",
   "text": "Waiter-path Get inconsistency: AtCapacity\u00d7Get blocks on connReqs (defer queued). When a connection arrives via waiter delivery (channel.go:142-147), the code checks idleTimeout on the delivered connection but does NOT check ping validity. The idle-conn fast path checks both; the waiter path skips ping. From run1 Q-04."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-05",
   "status": "ANSWERED — DR-005",
   "fault": [
    "F-01",
    "F-12"
   ],
   "trigger": "step-4 matrix walk",
   "text": "FactoryFail handling: factory failure during Get() at channel.go:155 returns error to caller without decrementing openingConns or notifying waiters. The openingConns counter can drift. Same for factory failure in NewChannelPool which calls c.Release() \u2014 but Release doesn't clean up connReqs either. Merged from run1 Q-03."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-06",
   "status": "OPEN",
   "fault": [
    "F-05",
    "F-14"
   ],
   "trigger": "step-4 matrix walk",
   "text": "SYS invariant violation: openingConns >= 0 can be broken. Close() at channel.go:211 unconditionally decrements openingConns with no guard against underflow. Double-close (UV-Close-duplication) or close-after-Release (UV-Close-out-of-order) can drive the counter negative. Close+Get race (UV-Close-contradiction) also possible. From run1 Q-06 and run2 Q-07/Q-08/Q-09."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-UV-01",
   "status": "OPEN",
   "fault": [
    "F-17",
    "F-18"
   ],
   "trigger": "step-3 checklist",
   "text": "Get undesired variants: UV-Get-commission (spurious Get \u2014 any goroutine with a pool reference can call Get()), UV-Get-value (subtle value fault \u2014 Get after Release returns ErrClosed but the error may be ignored). From run2 Q-12."
  }
 ],
